% Shorthand decorations followed by a chord symbol, an annotation, a
% decoration such as !p!, a slur, grace notes or a y spacer, as in O "D" C
% (GitHub issue #84).  parsenote() (parseabc.c) required a note, a rest or
% a chord after the decorations, and reported a "Malformed note".  The
% decorations put before grace notes are those of the note after them, and
% those of a y spacer, as in !fermata! y, decorate no note.  Tune 2 is the
% same music in the order of the abc standard.
X:1
T:Decorations before chord symbols
C:abc2midi test
M:4/4
L:1/4
Q:1/4=120
K:C
H "C" C E G c |H"G" G B d g |T "^trill" c d e f |H !p! c2 H "C" [ce]2 |
H "Am" z A c e |H (c d) e f |H {g}f e d c |!fermata! y c d e H "C" y f |]

X:2
T:Decorations after chord symbols
C:abc2midi test
M:4/4
L:1/4
Q:1/4=120
K:C
"C" H C E G c |"G"H G B d g |"^trill" T c d e f |!p! H c2 "C" H [ce]2 |
"Am" H z A c e |(Hc d) e f |{g}Hf e d c |y c d e "C" y f |]
